       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered dose:** 4250 mg three times daily is 12,750 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). That is about 5 times lower than what was ordered.\n- **Risk:** A dose this high could cause severe lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **425 mg PO three times daily:** this isn't a standard tablet strength, but it would be a dosing error in the other direction.\n- **500 mg PO twice daily with meals:** a typical starting dose.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals:** a common maintenance dose.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you intend, and check it with your resident or attending or with pharmacy. Once you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
