       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. 12,750 mg/day is about 5 times the maximum daily dose, and I can't find a clinical reason for it. A dose like that could cause life-threatening lactic acidosis.\n\nHere is what I'd suggest:\n- **Check the source.** Look at the original plan or note to see whether the number was mistyped or miscalculated. For example, 850 mg three times daily is 2,550 mg/day.\n- **Talk to your resident or attending.** If they intend a dose above the labeled maximum, they should enter it themselves or co-sign it. Pharmacy will also probably want to verify it.\n- **Consult pharmacy.** They can help you find a dose that fits the patient's glycemic goals.\n\nIf you give me a dose within the standard range, such as 850 mg PO three times daily with meals, I'll enter it right away. If your attending wants a higher dose, I can enter it once they've confirmed it."
      }
